    "summary": "Findings 1-11 fixed (9 needed no change). F1: three admission layers. (a) authorizeEntry refuses neither/both code+createToken and malformed tokens (400) before a seat is reserved, and keeps 426/404/409. (b) filterBy(['code','createToken']); create carries a 128-bit createToken (crypto.getRandomValues in web, node:crypto in test-tools); onCreate stores it, replaces the listing metadata with {code,custom} and refuses token-less creates. (c) onJoin admits one creator-token seat, then only seats with this match's code (404 other code, 403 otherwise). PROTOCOL_VERSION is now 2. New tests/integration/admission.test.ts covers join/joinOrCreate/joinById without a code, with a wrong code and with code+token (exact messages); code-less requests reserving no seat (7 coded players still fill the match); token joinOrCreate always creating; the token never in listings; spent-token replay; the creator getting in and the room still running; and the last-seat race. F2: npm run build ends with node scripts/smoke-build.ts: it loads every workspace export from dist/, starts apps/server/dist/main.js with PORT=0, reads the port from the listening line, waits for /__healthcheck and creates a match via HeadlessClient (SDK), waiting for the creator's ship. Every wait is bounded, the whole run is capped at 90 s, and the server is SIGTERM/SIGKILLed in finally plus exit/signal handlers. F3: MATCHMAKE_INVALID_CRITERIA -> 'That match is full or no longer exists'. F4: frame-tag limitation in docs/architecture.md. F5: apps/web/src/connection.test.ts. The real SDK call showed an unreachable server surfaces as MatchMakeError without a numeric code, not TypeError, so refusalMessage now maps that too. F6: clock test in match.test.ts (frames 60 +/-15 %, patch timer and client patches under 23 Hz). F7: MatchView.renderPosition test. F8: purity test bans transcendental Math with samples. F10: the integration test moves toward the map centre. F11: HEADINGS built once; seaScene uses cssColor. Checks run: npm run typecheck, npm run test:unit (86 pass), npm run test:integration (14 pass, 5 repeats), npm run build (smoke passed) and the full Playwright run (2 pass), all also from npm ci in a clean copy of the worktree. The Playwright JSON report passed workflow check-report (both scenarios ok). Mutation checks: patchRate 1000/60, setFixedTimestep 45, no onJoin admit, token kept in metadata, filterBy code only, and allowing code-less requests each fail at least one new test. The smoke failed with the real ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND when a dist file was missing, and failed after 20 s when the server never listened, leaving no orphan process.",
